  "title": "Disturbance gauntlet · Level 1: Hold 300 deg/s",
  "brief": "On the flywheel bench (an EV3 Medium on port 3 turning a 341.5 g disc of 50 mm radius and a pulley of 9 mm radius with a 200 g load on its cord), hold the flywheel at 300 deg/s through three step loads on the disc, each drawn per run: one starting between 1.0 and 1.5 s, one between 2.5 and 3.0 s, one between 4.0 and 4.5 s, each 4, 8 or 12 mN m, and each staying on. A run is read on the shaft's true speed every 1 ms from the first load to 2 s after the last, where it ends: IAE = the integral of |300 - speed| (deg), TV = the sum of the duty's changes (%). J = 0.8 x IAE / 7.3 + 0.2 x TV / 34.3; the run scores 100 x clamp(2 - J, 0, 1). Your own controller over dc() on Motor(3) (a built-in run(), track() or hold() scores 0); there is no ADRC/PID ratio yet (the comparison is not built: run your PID as a second Run challenge and read the two cards). Ten runs; pass: a mean of 60 or more and 8 runs through the window. Practice until LAB, DIST and COURSE ship. Par: IAE 7.3 deg, TV 34.3 %.",
